GROUND
Logical Ground Seqment sends Power message to Command and 
    Data Handling (CDH) subsystem (i.e. host).

HOST
Host powers on the Payload_X (emulator) using the power_up message. 

PAYLOAD
Payload_X recieves the power_up message. Then sends the ACK command with
    id of the power_up message

HOST
Host recieves ACK message and sends ID_Exchange message
Host polls until payload responds at 1 Hz, start ID_exchange time
    if (ID_exchange time >= ID_exchange timout){
        // flag or send an interrupt, using flag for simplicity
        timeout_flag = 1;
        break;
    }

PAYLOAD
Payload_X recieves the ID_exchange message, then processes the message
    That can look like verifying the SW_version, storing the UUID of the platform
        and the serial_number

Payload_X then send the ID_exchange message back to the host system
// POSSIBLE FAULT LOCATION
Payload_X just does not send back a message

HOST
Host handles the timeout and executes fault response
    if (timeout_flag){
        execute_fault_response(); // could look like remessaging, reference NACK
    }
Host recieves ID_Exchange message and send the offset message
/* might have to wait for the ACK for the offset message (message_ID = 5) or 
    just send it and continue? */
    
PAYLOAD
Payload_X recieves the Offset message
Payload_X sends the ACK message (message_ID = 5)

HOST
Host loops at 1Hz (every second) sending the PPS signal, Time message 
    and State message

PAYLOAD
Payload_X starts recieving PPS singal, Time message and State message at 1Hz
Payload_X starts sending Telemetry_Update message at 1Hz

HOST
Host starts sending space vehicle telemetry to the ground system.